---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout>
  <h1>Cloud Storage</h1>

  <p>By default, file uploads (evidence, certifications, attachments) are stored on the local filesystem (<code>EVIDENCE_STORAGE_PATH</code>). The platform supports switching to AWS S3 or Azure Blob via in-app settings.</p>

  <h2>Switching providers</h2>

  <p>Go to <strong>Settings → Storage</strong>. Select your provider and fill in the required credentials. The change takes effect immediately on the next request — no restart needed.</p>

  <h2>Local disk (default)</h2>

  <p>No configuration needed. Files stored at <code>EVIDENCE_STORAGE_PATH</code> (default <code>./.storage/evidence</code>). Suitable for single-container deployments.</p>

  <h2>AWS S3</h2>

  <p><strong>Required Settings:</strong></p>

  <table class="key-table">
    <tr>
      <th>Field</th>
      <th>Value</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>s3.bucket</code></td>
      <td>Your S3 bucket name</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>s3.region</code></td>
      <td>AWS region (e.g. <code>us-east-1</code>)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>s3.accessKeyId</code></td>
      <td>IAM user access key</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>s3.secretAccessKey</code></td>
      <td>IAM user secret key (encrypted at rest)</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <p><strong>Minimum IAM policy:</strong></p>

  <pre><code>{`{
  "Effect": "Allow",
  "Action": ["s3:PutObject", "s3:GetObject", "s3:DeleteObject", "s3:ListBucket"],
  "Resource": [
    "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket",
    "arn:aws:s3:::your-bucket/*"
  ]
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Azure Blob Storage</h2>

  <p><strong>Required Settings:</strong></p>

  <table class="key-table">
    <tr>
      <th>Field</th>
      <th>Value</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>azure.connectionString</code></td>
      <td>SAS URL or account key connection string (encrypted at rest)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><code>azure.containerName</code></td>
      <td>Blob container name (created automatically if it doesn't exist)</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <p><strong>SAS token requirements:</strong></p>

  <ul>
    <li>Service: <strong>Blob</strong></li>
    <li>Permissions: <strong>Read, Write, Delete, List, Create</strong></li>
    <li>Resource types: <strong>Container, Object</strong></li>
    <li>SAS token must include <code>srt=co</code> (Container + Object)</li>
  </ul>

  <p><strong>SAS URL format:</strong></p>

  <pre><code>BlobEndpoint=https://youraccount.blob.core.windows.net/;SharedAccessSignature=sv=2023-11-03&amp;ss=b&amp;srt=co&amp;sp=rwdlc&amp;se=2027-01-01T00:00:00Z&amp;sig=...</code></pre>

  <h2>Secrets security</h2>

  <p>Cloud storage credentials (S3 secret key, Azure connection string) are encrypted at rest using AES-256-GCM with your <code>APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>. They are never returned to the client (the settings page shows masked values). If <code>APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY</code> is rotated, decryption fails gracefully — storage falls back to local disk with a warning logged, rather than crashing.</p>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

  <table class="key-table">
    <tr>
      <th>Symptom</th>
      <th>Cause</th>
      <th>Fix</th>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Uploads fail after switching provider</td>
      <td>Credential format error</td>
      <td>Re-enter and save the credentials</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Azure: <code>InvalidBlobType</code> on upload</td>
      <td>Missing <code>srt=o</code> in SAS</td>
      <td>Regenerate SAS with Object resource type</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Provider didn't switch</td>
      <td>Cache hasn't invalidated</td>
      <td>Wait for next request (fingerprint-based invalidation, &lt; 1 request delay)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>Files lost after switching back to local</td>
      <td>Cloud files aren't synced</td>
      <td>Cloud storage and local disk are independent — migrate files manually if needed</td>
    </tr>
  </table>
</DocsLayout>
